<title>UK: Kvaerner wins Australian subsea contract.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner wins Australian subsea contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Kvaerner group said on Friday it had won a contract for designing and fabricating a complete subsea hardware package in Australia which would be worth in excess of A$ 50 ($39.34) million.</p>
<p>Kaverner said it was the largest subsea hardware contract ever placed with the group outside Norway.  </p>
<p>The package will be designed by Kvaerner Oilfield Products for Woodside Petroleum's Lamiraria and Corallina fields in Australia.</p>
<p>&quot;The scope includes wellhead systems, x-mas trees, manifolds, control systems, running tools, workover tools and tie-in systems,&quot; Kvaerner said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
